+\section{Phenotype-Measurement Audit}
+\label{sec:phenotype-audit}
+
+Phenotype target share is a hard class-1 fraction from a binary TinyCNN: class 0 is I--III;
+class 1 is IV--VI (P1) or V--VI (P4).  It has no abstention or calibration.  Real and
+generated images use the same RGB $[-1,1]$ preprocessing.  The saved evaluator reports only
+overall accuracy on the naturally imbalanced test-family images, and its construction did
+not explicitly seed PyTorch before weight initialization.
+
+We therefore ran a post-outcome, \emph{exploratory} sanity check using the same training
+recipe, frozen manifests, and an explicit torch seed.  It does not replace any confirmatory
+cell.  On real outer-test images, P1 target recall is 0\% in all three folds; P4 target recall
+is 0.0\%, 0.5\%, 0.0\%, 6.3\%, and 0.9\%, while source recall is 99.8--100\%.
+
